        "source": "import triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n@triton.jit\ndef softmax_stats(X, S, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    offsets = tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n    mask = offsets < N\n    x = tl.load(X + row * N + offsets, mask, other=-float('inf'))\n    mx = tl.max(x, 0)\n    exps = tl.exp(x - mx)\n    denom = tl.sum(exps, 0)\n    tl.store(S + row * 2, mx)\n    tl.store(S + row * 2 + 1, denom)\n\n@triton.jit\ndef softmax_apply(X, S, Y, TOTAL: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n    base_idx = tl.program_id(0) * BLOCK\n    offsets = tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n    i = base_idx + offsets\n    mask = i < TOTAL\n    row = i // N\n    x = tl.load(X + i, mask, other=0.0)\n    mx = tl.load(S + row * 2, mask, other=0.0)\n    denom = tl.load(S + row * 2 + 1, mask, other=1.0)\n    res = tl.exp(x - mx) / denom\n    tl.store(Y + i, res, mask)\n",
        "rationale": "Fix indexing in softmax_apply to compute row from global index i (i // N) for correct per-row loading of max and denom values. This corrects NaNs from invalid memory loads that caused verification failures. Preserve explicit masking in loads and stores to handle irregular shapes, ensuring correctness while maintaining occupancy and memory coalescing. No other changes to tile size or launch configuration to keep performance stable."
